  "notes": "{固|かた}まる is an intransitive godan verb meaning to harden, solidify, or become fixed. It covers both physical hardening and abstract finalization.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{固|かた}める→固める：01929_katameru⟧ (transitive — to harden something, to solidify)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{固|かた}まっている means \"is hardened\" or \"is set\" — the resulting state after solidification.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦セメント→セメント：19401_semento⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{固|かた}まる: cement hardens\n- ⟦{予定|よてい}→予定：00824_yotei⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{固|かた}まる: plans are finalized\n- ⟦{決意|けつい}→決意：07167_ketsui⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{固|かた}まる: one's resolve is set\n- ⟦{体|からだ}→体：00784_karada⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{固|かた}まる: body stiffens (from tension or fear)\n- ⟦{考|かんが}え→考え：00855_kangae⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{固|かた}まる: ideas take shape / become firm\n\nUSAGE:\nPhysical hardening (cement, glue, clay), abstract finalization (plans, decisions, opinions), and emotional/bodily stiffening (from nervousness or shock) are all natural uses.",
